                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="impl-notes" value="&lt;b&gt;Process vs. current implementation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;1. &lt;b&gt;Training window:&lt;/b&gt; the label is known only after the window, so phase A must use past windows; only phase B uses the last 2 hours.&lt;br&gt;2. &lt;b&gt;No real event log yet:&lt;/b&gt; the data is synthetic and each sequence is generated already in time order, so the 2-hour window and the time sorting (A1–A2, B1–B2) are not implemented.&lt;br&gt;3. &lt;b&gt;Label:&lt;/b&gt; in the synthetic data the label is drawn first and then drives the actions. For real data, &quot;called&quot; must be defined as a call within a fixed horizon after the window.&lt;br&gt;4. &lt;b&gt;Beyond the listed steps:&lt;/b&gt; the model also uses the first-state distribution π and Laplace smoothing (α = β = 1).&lt;br&gt;5. &lt;b&gt;Decision:&lt;/b&gt; likelihood only, without the prior P(call). A tie goes to &quot;Will not call&quot;. Event types outside the 11 states are not handled.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff8e1;strokeColor=#d6b656;dashed=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=12;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="680" y="1000" width="980" height="150" as="geometry" />
                </mxCell>
